; The ambiguity engine: the OCaml half of tools/ambiguity/, which the Python
; front end beside it runs as a subprocess.
;
; [Automaton] prepares what is being proved, [Stack_pool] and [Recognizer] own
; the exact GLR side, [Abstraction] and [Prover] the abstract one, [Search] the
; bounded concrete witness hunt, [History_filter] the refinement's history
; check, and [Output]/[Config] the caller-facing edges. [Run] is one
; invocation, dispatching to [Classes], [Proof] and [Concretize]; the
; executable is only its entry point, so tests link the library.
(library
 (name ambiguity_engine)
 (modules :standard \ ambiguity_search)
 (libraries unix str))

(executable
 (name ambiguity_search)
 (modules ambiguity_search)
 (libraries ambiguity_engine))
